# Live refresh: a file created by something else appears without an F5, and — the point of the
# whole design — the selection survives it.
#
# The merge exists because a load replaces FileListViewModel.Items and the view focuses the list
# when that happens. That is right for a navigation the user asked for and ruinous for a refresh
# nobody asked for, so a watcher-driven update diffs instead of clearing.

tree .
refresh
assert-count 8

# Something to lose. `write` puts a file on disk behind the app's back, exactly as another
# program would.
select notes.txt
assert-selected 1

write appeared.txt 1024
settle 600

# It arrived on its own — no refresh command anywhere above.
assert-row appeared.txt
assert-count 9

# And the selection is still there. Replace the merge with a reload and this goes red.
assert-selected 1

# Removal is the same path.
delete-permanent appeared.txt
settle 600
assert-no-row appeared.txt
assert-count 8

assert-not-launched
state
